dencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Godot v4.8.dev, since https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115998\n\n### System information\n\n Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2070 (NVIDIA; 32.0.16.1088) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-10750H CPU @ 2.60GHz (12 threads) - 15.82 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nShader previews can be set as breakpoints in the debugger in certain cases.\nIt happens because ScriptEditor doesn't properly check if a file is a Script when loading.\n\n<img width=\"417\" height=\"135\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/77debfe7-1f0f-4a11-970d-ea2856345f75\" />\n\nI have a fix for it as part of a pr, though its not dedicated just for this.\n\nIt can be cleared by clearing all breakpoints, but not deleting just this one. Or reloading while the conditions aren't met.\n\nIt doesn't seem to cause any issues, and isn't too commonly occurring, so its not critical IMO.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Have a shader\n2. Add it to a scene, in a material or somewhere\n3. Add a shader preview to the shader (any line)\n4. Save the project\n5. Close the shader in the shader editor\n6. Make sure the scene is open in the editor\n7. Reload the editor\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122142/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122142/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}